# ── VS Code Extension ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VS Code reads no .env file, so nothing here reaches the extension: the
# extension host runs in the environment VS Code starts in. The extension
# takes its provider, model, awsProfile and awsRegion settings from user or
# remote settings, never from a workspace. The bedrock provider signs
# through the AWS SDK's credential chain with the profile awsProfile names;
# with awsProfile empty, the chain starts from the extension host's
# environment (AWS_PROFILE and the other variables it reads). It calls
# Bedrock in the awsRegion setting's region; with that empty, in
# AWS_REGION, then us-east-1. No model credential is set anywhere.
